== complete -p prints the bash order and round-trips:
complete -o filenames -o nospace -d -A function -G '*.c' -W 'x y' -P 'pre' -S 'suf' -X '!*.h' -F fn foo
complete -b -e -A arrayvar -A setopt bar
complete -o dirnames -o plusdirs -a -c -d -k -v -A shopt -A signal baz
round-trip-ok
== complete -p prints an empty argument and round-trips:
complete -G '' -W '' -P '' -S '' -X '' -C '' foo
round-trip-ok
== complete -p prints an empty function name bare:
complete -F  foo
